<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.AnnotationModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:ann="org.blockml.bml.annotation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:diag="org.blockml.bml.diagnostic"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>AnnotationModel</name>
  <type>doc:AnnotationModel</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to Annotation namespaces and facets</is>

  <documentation>
    Annotations formalize directive namespaces. They are orthogonal to the Definition meta-model
    (org.blockml.bml.definition.*) — they do not describe block structure, members, or constraints.
    Naming overlap (Property, Aggregation, …) classifies directive form only;
    Annotation.Property is not def:PropertyDefinition.

    Every BML-semantic xmlns prefix resolves to either a Package (type addressing) or a concrete
    Annotation (directives). preferredAlias is authoring convention only (bml, scad) — the BOM
    stores the Annotation FQN, never the XML prefix. Document default xmlns and xsi:schemaLocation
    use http://blockml.org/bml (→ bml.xsd); legacy schema URIs are obsolete. BML-semantic xmlns:bml
    must target ann:BmlAnnotation — never a schema URL.

    Branch shape (core:Annotation):
    • preferredAlias : Text
    • directives : Directive[]
    • Directive — name = local name
      · Member (name="*") → Property | Aggregation | Association | Capability
      · Element → Document | Summary | Examples | Example | Value (fixed names)
      · Attribute — fixed names (id, each, with, …)

    Concrete annotations:
    • org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation (bml) — language directives; see doc:BmlDirectives
    • Domain annotations (e.g. com.machineblocks.bml.annotation.ScadAnnotation, scad) — members,
      value facets, prose facets, example facets

    Directive match:
    • Attribute / Element (incl. fixed Document, Summary, Examples, Example, Value) —
      localName == directive.name
    • Member subtypes — name="*"; any local name under the annotation; kind from the Member subtype

    Parent context for *:value:
    • Direct child of &lt;properties&gt; → Member (Annotation.Property) when declared
    • Nested under a property element → Value facet (Annotation.Value) — same property identity,
      not member scad:myProp
    Never means a renamed member QName.

    Parent context for *:example:
    • Prefixed child of &lt;examples&gt; → Annotation.Example (sibling of canonical &lt;example&gt;)
    • Unprefixed &lt;example&gt; → StructuralDefinition.Example
    Prefer sibling *:example for 1:1 BML↔target pairs; use *:examples for independent target-only
    sets. Annotation facets never replace required canonical documentation / value / examples slots.

    Property value facets multiply PropertyDefinition.value along the Annotation namespace axis
    ("" | Annotation FQN). Cross-namespace faceting is valid; same-namespace self-faceting is
    forbidden. Duplicate namespace on one property → BML_DUPLICATE_PROPERTY_VALUE. Facets do not
    satisfy or replace the canonical &lt;value&gt; for BML instance semantics unless a renderer
    explicitly prefers an Annotation facet.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="core:Annotation" relation="Defines">
      Annotation branch — Directive taxonomy and preferredAlias.
    </see>
    <see type="ann:BmlAnnotation" relation="SeeAlso">
      Concrete language Annotation (preferredAlias bml).
    </see>
    <see type="def:PropertyDefinition" relation="SeeAlso">
      Value-field Annotation facets on properties.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:BmlNamespace" relation="SeeAlso">
      Package vs Annotation xmlns targets and domain.bml.* layout.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:BmlDirectives" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — bml: language directive placement and semantics.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_DUPLICATE_PROPERTY_VALUE" relation="SeeAlso">
      Duplicate value facet on the same Annotation namespace.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
